course: dictionary
lesson: 12102
title: Big words for thinking
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cognition is a long, formal word for thinking. It means all the work your brain does to know, learn, remember and understand things.
explain: Paying attention, remembering a phone number and solving a puzzle are all parts of cognition. «Mia's cognition was sharp, so she solved the maths puzzle in seconds.» Here the word points to how well her brain was thinking.
explain: Scientists use the word when they study thinking in people and in animals. «Scientists studied the cognition of crows and found they can solve tricky puzzles.» Cognition is a noun; the describing word is cognitive.
fact: Cognition is a noun meaning the mental processes of knowing, thinking, learning, remembering and understanding.
fact: Cognition can also mean the ability to think and understand.
fact: Cognition is a formal word used in science and psychology.
fact: «Cognitive» is the adjective: «cognitive skills» means thinking skills.
fact: Doctors may test the cognition of older people, and scientists study animal cognition in crows and chimps.
exercise: «Scientists study animal cognition in crows and chimps.» What does cognition mean here? | Running fast | Sleeping deeply | *Thinking, learning and remembering | A type of food
exercise: What is the describing word (adjective) for cognition? | thinking | knowledge | *cognitive | cognition
exercise: «Doctors may test the cognition of older people.» What are the doctors checking? | *How well the brain thinks, remembers and understands | What the patient ate for lunch | How much the patient weighs | How tall the patient is
test: «The puzzle needed good cognition, so Sam used his memory and logic.» What does cognition mean? | A kind of puzzle book | A loud noise | A cold wind | *The mental processes of thinking and understanding
test: Which sentence uses cognition correctly? | The cognition was dark and wet. | The cognition ran fast to the shop. | Cognition is a bright red flower. | *Her cognition was strong, so she remembered every word of the poem.
exam: Which meaning fits cognition best? | A type of fish | Strong muscles for running | *The mental processes of knowing, thinking, learning and remembering | The brightness of a light
